# ============================================================================
# Personal exploratory fine-tuning track. Code, small OOD test batteries, and
# small report JSONs ARE tracked (see personal_finetune/README.md). The Dutch
# track's own bulk train/eval JSONL data stays excluded below (hosted on the
# farahelmashad/personal-pii-tamerbert-generalization-data Kaggle dataset
# instead, and regenerable via personal_finetune/augmentation/) -- but the
# French and English tracks' bulk data IS tracked directly in git (see their
# sections below, 2026-08-19), so those two need no separate Kaggle upload to
# use directly. Large cached raw-prediction dumps from each trial run stay
# excluded for all tracks.
# ============================================================================
personal_finetune/**/__pycache__/
personal_finetune/tamerbert_data/*.jsonl
personal_finetune/*/outputs/**/raw_predictions.json
new_data/
TamerBERT.zip
# TamerBERT/ intentionally NOT ignored (2026-08-18): the English track needs
# train.jsonl (template recovery source), pii_table.py (Dutch reference
# generator), and org_data/*.pdf (the 5 real reference documents) directly
# from the repo rather than only via the separate Kaggle-hosted copy.

# French track (personal_finetune/french/): bulk train/eval JSONL data is
# now tracked directly in git too (2026-08-19, explicit override of the
# original Kaggle-only-hosting convention, so a plain clone/pull has
# everything needed for training/eval without regenerating it) -- only
# the CSV audit dumps (diagnostic tool output, not training/eval data,
# regenerable via `python pii_table_fr.py --audit`) stay excluded.
personal_finetune/french/*.csv

# English track (personal_finetune/english/): same as French above --
# bulk train/eval JSONL data tracked directly in git; only CSV audit
# dumps excluded.
personal_finetune/english/*.csv

